I have seen the usefulness of pets and it is good!

My gnomish healer started out normally enough.  But this time I kept my
dog and let it do all the killing.  There were some close calls
involvng weres, but praying tooking care of any lycanthropy.  There was
a coaligned altar on D1, a nonalgined altar on D3, and a nonaligned
altar on D5, right next to a tool shop.

At this point I was still XL 1 with 12 hp.  I let my super dog kill
mimics and steal everything in the shop including a magic whistle, bag
of tricks, key, oil lamp, and towel.  I took a risk and converted the
atlar by the shop.  Everything went ok, but I didn't get any artifacts.


Originally I'd gone to the Mines, but the first level was dark.  With
my oil lamp at hand I went in and let my dog slaughter every gnome and
dwarf in sight.  I managed to get to Minetown *still* at XL 1, with
almost $2000!  But close to the temple a homoculous put my dog to
sleep.  I panicked and fried it with a fire horn (of which I had two
from the tool shop), and went to XL two!  I bought 4 or 5 points of
protection, let my pet kill every mimic and guard, and stole assorted
spellbooks, armor, and tools from the shopkeepers.  I got a silver
saber from the watch captain, an uncursed magic lamp from the tool
shop, and enough armor to take me to AC -1.  I used credit cloning to
get a ton of gold and give myself $8k credit in each shop.  This seemed
like a good idea at the time, but came back to hurt me later.

I bought two more points of protection (having risen to XL3), and did I
mention the temple was coaligned?  Hermes gave me Vorpal Sword.  I
decided to bring both long sword and saber to basic and switch as
appropriate, with Vorpal being my main weapon.

I went back up to the main dungeon and on the Oracle level I found a
bones pile of a monk who died on a magic trap.  He had a cloak of magic
resistance which was uncursed, and a pet saddled pony.  At this point I
had a super dog and a super cat.  I tamed the pony and rode it around,
but it died pretty quickly.  I used the fountains to make water which
became holy water, blessed my magic lamp, and got a wish that went to a
blessed +2 SDSM.

Now with the important magic resistance, reflection, and an AC of -12
or so, I went to Sobokan.  It was fairly unevenful.  I brought my pets
with me, a first for me  because I find pets to be very annoying in
Sobokan.  But this time they were quite helpful and kept my XL low.  In
Sobokan I tamed a horse that became a warhorse, but he died fighting
for me in the treasure room.  He kept hitting a spotted jelly until it
killed him.

On the last level I claimed a BoH and blessed it.  There was no gold
because I had used a tooled horn to scare a giant mimic and that had
woken up a rock mole in the treasure room.  Oops!

I went back to the mines and headed for Mine Bottom.  One level before
bottom I found another bones file, this one of a Valk who had died to 3
sergeants because she lacked sleep resistance, though she had a BoH and
lots of scrolls and potions.  She also had boots of jumping, boots of
water walking, and gauntlets of dexterity!  Whew!

I took the good stuff to my stash and cleared out Bottom.  I had the
hardest time finding the luckstone, and picked up a lodestone by
mistake.  This was the version with no cellar, and the luckstone was in
the part that is hard to get into unless you are carrying very little.
At this point I also found a polymorph trap.  My dog became a rock
troll and my cat became a winged gargoyle.  The WG got the luckstone
for me and I blessed it.

So ... I had cleared out Mine Bottom and Sobokan, had a BoH, SDSM,
CoMR, Vorpy, and lots of UnID'ed stuff from that bones pile.  I wanted
to used the general store in Minetown to price Id stuff, but I had a
ton of credit and didn't know how to price ID on credit.  Spoilers
indicated shopkeepers gave 90% of an items value, but when I offered a
ring of teleport control I was offered $100 in credit.  That isn't 90%.

I tried to drain my credit by buying a plate mail and throwing it.  I
erased about $300 credit per buy and throw but it was slow going.  Then
I had the genius idea to throw Vorpy and buy it back.  I threw it for
$450 credit and the shopkeeper wanted .... $12,000 for it back!  I
wasn't having that and summoned my pets (who were locked up for the
safety of the remaining people of Minetown).  They made short work of
the shop keeper, but now I had no way to price Id stuff.

After thinking about it more, a better solution would have been to
throw a *precious gem* and buy it back.  But that never occured to me
until after I threw Vorpy.

Fortunately, I was able to write some ID scrolls and bless them with
found magic markers.  One of them Id'ed my entire inventory and most of
the UnID'ed stuff.  I sacced for luck and left Minetown.

Back in the regular dungeon, I found some throne rooms and a leprechuan
hall.  My pets cleared these and I got one wish from each throne!  I
wished for B+oID and B+oCM.  My identifying problems were over and I no
longer worried about my non-eating gargoyle going wild.

I found the portal to Ludios and the Quest, but was not ready for
either.  Farther down I found 2 more general stores, but I let my pets
kill the shopkeepers for the money since I had ID.

On D19 there was another Neutral altar, so I decided that would be my
new Stash.  My old one was on D5 still.  Two levels down was Medusa's
level and a Titan.  He of course summoned monsters, but after a long
fight and burning Elbereth twice, I killed him and let my rock troll
eat his corpse.

On the way back up I found another poly trap and my rock troll became a
glass golem.  I had a ring of teleport control, so I used that plus my
?oT to transfer my stash from D5 to D19.  I used up both markers to get
my AC to a respectable -20, but I was still at XL 10 because I'd let my
pets do most of the fighting.  I took out Medusa, who turned my glass
golem into a weaker stone golem.  One leve down was a regular level.
Here, my glass golem was eaten by at trapper!  Nooo!  One level after
that was a hell-type level where a Minotaur almost killed me!  I was
down to 15 hp and zapped him with a wand of poly instead of a wand of
teleport.  Fortunately, he turned into a homoculous and I escaped
alive.

I played poly trap with my remaining pet and ended up with a baby gray
dragon who wouldn't poly because of his innate MR.  I thought about
abandoning it (had my hopes set on something stronger immediately), but
I decided to let Puff the Magic Dragon tag along.  This turned out to
be a good idea.

In Ludios, I found several !oGL plus a succubus.  I took all the gold
and got to XL 13, and Puff  grew to a level 22 Gray Dragon with 176 hp!
 Wow!  That's pretty darn good.

I spent many turns after that looking for wraiths or anything to gain a
level.  Eventually I did, and went to the quest again.  I had an oMB so
the water creatures didn't scare me, and I had BoWW so I wasn't going
to get my stuff wet.

I donated all the Ludios gold to the Chaotic priest and got to -2 naked
AC.

I'd heard the Cyclops was scary and a /oDeath, Sleep, and Elbereth were
reccomended.  At first he just taunted me and teleported so I got lazy
and lost 3 levels to him before I got serious and burned Elbereth on
the stairs up.  After killing Cyclops I managed to get to XL 13 again,
but was still a level down from the encounter.  Lesson learned - don't
fool around with Cyclops when he has the Staff.

But now I had the Staff!  I enchanted it to +6 and quickly got to
skillled in quarterstaff.  I tamed an Olag Hai and took it and Puff to
the Castle level.  I learned the tune, but a soldier with a /oStrike
blew apart the drawbridge and killed Trollbabe - who had my
Ogresmasher!

I cleared the castle easily with my Staff and when I got the WoW I
didn't know what to wish for.  I already had GoD, BoWW, CoMR, SDSM, and
a HoB I had found in Mine Bottom.  I had +oID and +oCM, plus remove
curse and other useful spells.  I had rings of levitation and conflict,
but I didn't want to wish for free action or slow digestion because I
usually find those anyway.

So I didn't wish for anything and stashed the wand.  I used CM to tame
an Aleax and a purple worm.  The worm was great at killing stuff, but
the Aleax was much less impressive.  I shortly abandoned the Aleax on
my stash level.

I decided I would ride Puff using one of my three saddles.  Yeah, it
took  me this long to think of it.  I normally don't ride so this would
be fun!  After all I could be very fast, carry more, etc.  I got the
saddle and rode Puff from my D19 stash back to Medusa.  One level down
a Black Dragon disintegrated Puff *and* the precious saddle.  *Gasp*
My best pet!  And the one I had had almost the whole game.  At this pet
I was getting tired of pets because the seemed to be much less
effective than before.  I still had a pet Purple Worm eating stuff, but
I got tired of waitng for it to finish eating and left it.

In the VotD I found Magic Mapping, another spellbook I had been
thinking about wishing for.  I baited Wraiths to the Castle but got
exactle zero wraith corpses.  At this point I was XL 16.  Before going
further I used a wish for unholy water and made *more*  unholy water.
Then I cursed some ?oDA and proofed all my armor.

I needed to go rememorize ID and remove curse, but I decided to plunge
into Hell first.  I was able to cast MMapping with a failure rate of
83%, which was good enough.  I killed Asmodeus and Juiblex, and went to
Baazelbub's level, but he fled from me.  I used this opportunity to go
back to my stash and relearn some spells.  I peformed alchemy too, and
got my hp over 200.

I went back down and apparently missed Baazelbub entirely somehow.  I
found Vlads and cleared it out, get the AoLS and a ring of slow
digestion.  Now I only need free action!

In Orcus town I found the Staff to be very ineffective against shades,
but they didn't drain my speed once.  No one could drain my levels
thankfully, I was only XL 18 at this point.  Before I could kill Orcus
he read a scroll of teleportation.  Blinding myself confirmed he was
not on the level anymore.  Great, so now I had no idea where he was!  I
continued down and mapped most levels.  When I ran out of pow I relied
on my magic lamp (I got another one somewhere) and patience to find the
stairs down.  Lichs proved to be very annoying this game.  It seemed
like every other spell was a curse spell, but I had almost 30 holy
waters so I was prepared.  I always go holy water crazy when I get
boots of water walking.  :D

This game BOTTOM was on D47, and I found the vibrating square quickly!
That's a first!  Recently I dug up the entire bottom level to find that
square!  (Of course I probably missed the message because I was so busy
digging.  Eventually I destroyed every wall on the level and lit the
whole room.)

Anyway, I dropped a Hawaiian Shirt on the square for distinctiveness
and teleported back to my  stash.  I stored more junk (included 45 K
rations and 33 C rations, 10 oil lamps, and something like 20 unicorn
horns).

I recharged both magic markers and enchanted my armor to +4/+5, except
for the boots because I ran out of charges.  I also wrote ?oGD when my
markers got really low.  My AC went to -39!  I could've done it sooner,
but I didn't really need to, the Staff was killing most things so fast.

At this point I *still* didn't have free action so I wished for it.  I
gathered up all my stuff for the final descent, put my BoH in a sack
for curse protection, and headed back down the long way.  I found Orcus
on Asmodeus's level.  He gave me an empty wand of death and I was out
of charging scrolls.
I found Baazlebub one level below in Juiblex's swamp.  I didn't even
know he was still alive!  I'd completely forgotten he'd fled and I'd
continued on.

I finished mapping every level, now that I had 180ish pow and over 400
hp.  Yes, the pow is low, but I spent most of the game with under 100
so to me it was a lot.  I'd also maxed out all my stats and had +4 GoD
and a +5 HoB.  My XL was only 21 because I'd encounter much fewer
succubi than usual, and no amulets of change had been discovered.
Plus, I had rotten luck getting wraith corpses.  Har har.  :D

I grabbed the Bell and Candle at Vlads where I'd left em and found I
had to drop some of my 44 K Rations.  Ok, so  that is too much food.

Unburnded, I headed to the real tower and cleared it out.  A demilich
woke everyone up, but that everyone included two cockatrices.  2
cockatrices plus a ring of conflict equaled a lot of statues.

At the top of the tower I had some trouble getting the Book.  The first
thing Rodney did was cast Double Trouble.  Then he summoned monsters,
including a MMF, and refused to stop levitating over water, so I was
afraid to kill him because I didn't want the Book in the water.
Speaking of water, I did get my Ogresmasher back using a wand of cold
and a pickaxe.

Eventually I killed all the Rodneys and high-tailed it outta there,
avoidng the MMF, and running for BOTTOM.  At Bottom I opened the
sanctum and met a Demilich and a master lich, both of which woke up
everything.  Lichs are sooo annoying that way.

So I used conflict and a handy cockatrice corpse to kill my way though
the graveyard.  After that I switched to the staff and headed for the
big room with the temple.  My next step was into a pit, so it was a
good thing I switched weapons when I did!

Getting the amulet took a lot less time than usual, thanks to my c
corpse, and left lots of fine art.  When I stoned the high priest the
Amulet was on the ground by the statue instead of in the statue.  That
was interesting.  I left the sanctum and headed back up....

and had the most frustrating ascent to date!  It was even worse than my
lawful samurai!  I was ok from level 47 to 30 something.  But then, I
COULD NOT GET PAST JUBILEX's SWAMP!!!!

Every single time I got to the stairs I was thrown back.  And the swamp
was fillling up with gremlins.  Then I was waylaid two levels down by
the Wizard who summoned a group of monsters including 2 arch liches and
a MMF.  I had been keeping the polymorphing to a minimum (just that
minotaur by accident) to keep the game challenging, but I lost patience
when I saw all those monsters.  I broke out my wands of poly zapped
away.  Apparently you can't poly arch liches though.  And those arch
liches kept cursing me!  Argh!

I finally got away but I was extremely irrate at this point and my
healer fainted from hunger on 3 separate occasions because I was
focusing on gettiing out of Hell and not on his hunger.  Fortunately,
nothing could kill me with the Staff in my possession.  And then I took
out a bunch of food and PAID attention!

Oh, and one of those arch-liches summoned Yeenghou, but it didn't save
him.  Muhahahaha!  Though I was terrified for a moment because I saw
the purple & and thought "Demogorgon".

During all this fighting, summoning, fainting, and gremlin
reproduction, I made it to Asmodeuses stairs up many many times.  But
that mysterious force would not let me up.  It had me mistaken for a
lawful character.

But there was no way I was letting the Man hold me down.  I was going
to ascend or kill my healer in a blaze of glory, and since hungerless
regen was keeping me alive, ascension was the only option.

(No I wasn't trying to kill my healer.  I *was* extremely annoyed with
the mysterious force and therefore not nearly as careful as I usually
am)

Then the most amazing thing happened.  I stood on the stairs up, hit
"<", and was at the Valley of the Dead.  O.o

I literally cheered when I got there.  There aren't words to describe
how happy I was to get away from the annoying mysterious force.

The rest of the ascension went pretty smoothly.  I was cursed a lot by
black auras, but Rodney didn't dare show his face until Earth, and I
had plenty of holy water plus remove curse at my disposal.

When I got to the stairs up on D1, I checked to make sure I had the
right amulet.  Then I wished for a blessed spellbook of cure sickness,
think I might need it against Pestilence.  Yep, I went the whole game
without the special healer spell for my healer.  Then again, I didn't
get sick or slimed once durig the game either.

On earth I quickly killed Rodney.  Well, pretty quickly.  I was
conserving my last 3 wand of death charges for Astral so I had to whack
him a lot with the Staff.  A confused ?oGD showed me the way and I went
to Air wearing =oconflict and =oLev.  I was engulfed by an elemental
once on Air, but it's damage couldnt' match my AC plus regeneration.
Air and Fire were a lot of going on space, going through a lot of
messages and then going one space again.

On water, I ignored all the water species and went to the center of the
screen.  I read a confused ?oGD and headed in that general direction.
I actually saw the portal in a bubble so I took off my conflict before
I got to Astral.

On Astral I put on free action and slow digestion.  I took out the two
master liches and went  to far left.  This was Pestilence, who I was
really ready for.  I used my last wand of death charges killing
Pestilence and then carved my way through the left side using the
Staff.  Angels and Priest are no match  for level drain!

Turns out, I guessed right on my first go.  Rather than clear out
Astral I offered the amulet and ascended one of the tougher nethack
classes.  Yay!

Joeb, neutral male gnomish Healer






